%description:
Tests the dielectric loss of DielectricObstacleLoss for a metal: one transmission
crosses a single plate of copper that is 2 mm thick, at three frequencies. Reflection
loss is switched off. The plate is thicker than EPSILON (1 mm), below which the two
intersections of the path are the same Coord and the object takes no loss.

Copper has the resistivity 1.68e-8 Ohm m and a relative permittivity and permeability
of 1. Its loss tangent 1 / (2 pi f rho eps_0) is very large, so the power decays as
exp(-2 z / delta) with the skin depth delta = sqrt(2 rho / (2 pi f mu_0)) of a good
conductor. Expected values:

  2.4 GHz: delta = 1.332 um, loss 13046 dB (factor 0)
  10 MHz:  delta = 20.63 um, loss 842.111 dB
  100 kHz: delta = 206.3 um, loss 84.211 dB

At 2.4 GHz the factor exp(-2 z / delta) is below the smallest double, so it is 0 and
the plate blocks the signal.

Before the repair (BD-49 of the defect list), copper had the resistivity
1.68 Ohm m and the permittivity and permeability NaN, so the factor was NaN and the
ASSERT of computeDielectricLoss() failed in debug mode.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: test.ned
import inet.environment.common.PhysicalEnvironment;
import inet.physicallayer.wireless.common.medium.RadioMedium;
import inet.test.unittest.lib.ObstacleLossTest;

network ObstacleLossTestNetwork
{
    submodules:
        physicalEnvironment: PhysicalEnvironment;
        radioMedium: RadioMedium;
        test: ObstacleLossTest;
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: environment.xml
<environment>
    <object position="min 4.9 -5 -5" orientation="0 0 0" shape="cuboid 0.002 10 10" material="copper"/>
</environment>
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = ObstacleLossTestNetwork
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-event-banners = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = "%l %C: "
**.cmdenv-log-level = INFO

*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMinX = -10m
*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMinY = -10m
*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMinZ = -10m
*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMaxX = 20m
*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMaxY = 10m
*.physicalEnvironment.spaceMaxZ = 10m
*.physicalEnvironment.config = xmldoc("environment.xml")
*.radioMedium.backgroundNoise.power = -100dBm
*.radioMedium.obstacleLoss.typename = "DielectricObstacleLoss"
*.radioMedium.obstacleLoss.enableReflectionLoss = false

*.test.frequencies = "2.4e9 1e7 1e5"
*.test.txX = 0m
*.test.txY = 0m
*.test.txZ = 0m
*.test.rxX = 10m
*.test.rxY = 0m
*.test.rxZ = 0m
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%extraargs: -s
%subst: /\n<!> No more events, simulation completed.*?\n//
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "obstacle loss at" test.out > filtered.out
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: filtered.out
INFO (ObstacleLossTest)ObstacleLossTestNetwork.test: obstacle loss at 2.4e+09 Hz: inf dB
INFO (ObstacleLossTest)ObstacleLossTestNetwork.test: obstacle loss at 1e+07 Hz: 842.111 dB
INFO (ObstacleLossTest)ObstacleLossTestNetwork.test: obstacle loss at 100000 Hz: 84.211 dB
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%not-contains: stdout
undisposed object:
%not-contains: stdout
-- check module destructor
